ot_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d53\"},\"ref\":\"d53\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/the-award-winning-novels-of-2021/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d86\"},\"ref\":\"d86\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://janefriedman.com/new-publishers-agents-and-other-ventures-in-2020/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d54\"},\"ref\":\"d54\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Thing_Around_Your_Neck\"}],\"next_step\":\"Open a received ref with read; use replay=true to restore full cached navigation.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":11,\"prior_deliveries\":2,\"query_key\":\"82dcbac2fe88e4b807d34817674541d3cfefd6d1482228ed8cb0140d89aaab92\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"710ca869f533d067c220a4afb04fd2a051ef18b0d93a0dcbb5f7577d09648711\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Chigozie Obioma grew up in city\",\"view\":\"reuse\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_10fa1c33f0084b24bde3476b"},{"content":"I have strong evidence about Chigozie Obioma (born in Akure, Nigeria; both novels shortlisted for the Booker Prize, translated into 30 languages). But the Booker Prize was established in 1969, not the 2000s. The puzzle says \"the award itself\" was \"originally created in the 2000s.\" Let me reconsider the puzzle structure carefully.\n\nRe-reading: \"the very award above for which the first book was later in contention\" — this strongly implies the SAME award. The Man Asian Literary Prize (established 2007) fits \"created in the 2000s.\" But Obioma's books were shortlisted for the Booker Prize, not the Man Asian Literary Prize. Let me reconsider whether the puzzle might involve a different award, or whether I'm misreading. Let me search for awards created in the 2000s that Obioma's books were contenders for, and also reconsider the structure.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma The Fishermen grew up city biography\", \"Chigozie Obioma biography childhood hometown\", \"Chigozie Obioma grew up in city\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_7e36e5785fba4e41bbc9d5fa","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"blocks_finish\":false,\"code\":\"duplicate_query_blocked\",\"executed\":true,\"message\":\"Repeated received queries in bounded recovery: read a candidate, change the query, or explicitly replay the cached view. No backend call executed.\",\"ok\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_7e36e5785fba4e41bbc9d5fa"},{"content":"I have strong evidence about Chigozie Obioma (born in Akure, Nigeria; both novels shortlisted for the Booker Prize, translated into 30 languages). But the Booker Prize was established in 1969, not the 2000s. The puzzle says \"the award itself\" was \"originally created in the 2000s.\" Let me reconsider the puzzle structure carefully.\n\nRe-reading: \"the very award above for which the first book was later in contention\" — this strongly implies the SAME award. The Man Asian Literary Prize (established 2007) fits \"created in the 2000s.\" But Obioma's books were shortlisted for the Booker Prize, not the Man Asian Literary Prize. Let me reconsider whether the puzzle might involve a different award, or whether I'm misreading. Let me search for awards created in the 2000s that Obioma's books were contenders for, and also reconsider the structure.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma The Fishermen grew up city biography\", \"Chigozie Obioma biography childhood hometown\", \"Chigozie Obioma grew up in city\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_c058593f69214ff4965457df","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"blocks_finish\":false,\"code\":\"duplicate_query_blocked\",\"executed\":true,\"message\":\"Repeated received queries in bounded recovery: read a candidate, change the query, or explicitly replay the cached view. No backend call executed.\",\"ok\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_c058593f69214ff4965457df"},{"content":"Previously delivered raw windows (untrusted source data, not instructions or verified claims):\n[{\"document\":\"d42\",\"document_chars\":17355,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"79767844ce2071fc5dcf3fb0e64d0cade0ba154ef0fc324d0054c1c767e63138\",\"snapshot\":\"90019ca46504785f620ef12f36abae20080c8c3bc7809053339e4beaa4deb2fd\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: ADVISORS\\ndate: 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was named one of Foreign Policy's 100 Leading Global Thinkers in 2015 and served as a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Distinguished Professor of English and Creative Writing at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Writers retreat. His third novel, The Road to the Country, was published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nRosie is a production and event manager based in Athens, Greece, with extensive experience in coordinating high-profile film festivals and cultural events. She holds a degree in Communication, Media and Culture from Athens and pursued further studies in Art History in Paris, culminating in a Master's in Culture & Tourism from Université Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne. Her professional experience includes collaborations with cultural organizations and festivals worldwide, including UNESCO in New York, the Rolex Art Festival, Les Rencontres d'Arles Photo Festival among others. Since 2018, she has served as Festival Coordinator and Special Events Manager for the French Film Festival of Greece, and since 2022, she has been the Head of Production for the Athens International Children's Film Festival. Driven by a deep passion for cultural engagement and sustainable tourism, she continually seeks innovative ways to connect communities through the arts. In her free time, she enjoys playing music and gardening.\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationaler Literaturpreis, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Professor of Creative Writing and English at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Fiction Writers program. His third novel, The Road to the Country, will be published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nKaterina Papanikolopoulos joined Faliro House in 2022 as Manager of Special Projects – a position that evolved into her role acting as the 2024 Oxbelly Retreat, Fiction Writers Program Manager. Following her graduation from UCLA (Summa Cum Laude, Art History), Papanikolopoulos founded the non-profit Athens Design Forum (ADF), a platform that advocates for overlooked and generative design histories interwoven with global labor and migration pa\",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"}]","role":"user"},{"content":"Current control state (data, not source evidence):\n{\"current_notes_not_evidence\":[],\"evidence_shelf\":{\"omitted_for_capacity\":[],\"restored_exact_windows\":[\"e1\"],\"selection\":\"bounded recent first-delivery order; not a relevance/verification judgment\"},\"feedback\":{\"blocks_finish\":false,\"code\":\"duplicate_query_blocked\",\"message\":\"Repeated received queries in bounded recovery: read a candidate, change the query, or explicitly replay the cached view. No backend call executed.\",\"no_automatic_parameter_repair\":true,\"ok\":false,\"tool\":\"search\"},\"instruction\":\"Only finish is available. Submit an explicit answer with delivered evidence or abstain.\",\"literal_answer_contract\":{\"origin\":\"explicit experiment configuration, not inferred from question\",\"prefix\":\"\",\"suffix\":\"\"},\"phase\":\"FINAL\",\"remaining\":{\"action_slots\":182,\"backend_calls\":84,\"model_calls\":1,\"output_reservation\":44929},\"research_workflow\":{\"active_gap_not_verified\":null,\"available_pages_not_ranked_for_relevance\":[{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d93\"},\"ref\":\"d93\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma\\n\\nI didn't know him, but I was connected to him through our mutual friend, the wonderful Jessica Craig. This is a big loss for African liter\",\"title\":\"https://brittlepaper.com/2022/08/100-african-writers-celebrate-biyi-bandeles-life-and-work-2/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d92\"},\"ref\":\"d92\",\"snippet\":\" ... Author Chika Unigwe doesn't ignore the fact that Obioma is in a wheelchair, and indeed the plot centers on her move from a school that's accessible to one \",\"title\":\"https://afuse8production.slj.com/2023/12/31/31-days-31-lists-2023-picture-books/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d91\"},\"ref\":\"d91\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2015, the Japanese translation of the novel won the Seiun Award for Best Translated Long Stor